## Auto-provision Lakebase registry on deploy

Context: First install required a pre-existing Lakebase database and a
manual Settings → Registry → Initialize click. make deploy now creates
missing UC/Lakebase resources and initializes the registry schema.

Changes:

1. scripts/_internal/_init-lakebase-registry.py
   Serverless warehouse picker and LakebaseRegistryStore.initialize() CLI.
2. tests/units/scripts/test_init_lakebase_registry.py
   Picker and initialize wrapper contracts.
3. scripts/deploy.sh
   Resolve empty WAREHOUSE_ID; ensure UC catalog/schema; call setup-lakebase.sh;
   initialize registry before grants.
4. scripts/deploy.config.sh
   Document create-if-missing and empty warehouse default.
5. scripts/bootstrap/setup-lakebase.sh
   Drop the UI Initialize next-step (deploy does it).
6. scripts/bootstrap/lakebase-perms.sh
   Comments: schema is created at deploy time.
7. docs/DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md / docs/deployment.md / docs/dab-reference.md / docs/INFO.md
   First deploy no longer requires a manual Initialize click.

