## Skip Lakebase recreate and owner-only initialize on existing registries

Context: make deploy against an Autoscaling project (not database/instances)
tried POST /database/instances and failed. Replaying initialize() as the
human deployer hit "must be owner of table" on app-owned tables.

Changes:

1. scripts/bootstrap/setup-lakebase.sh
   Treat an existing /api/2.0/postgres/projects/{name} as already provisioned.
2. scripts/_internal/_init-lakebase-registry.py
   Skip initialize() when store.is_initialized() is true.
3. tests/units/scripts/test_init_lakebase_registry.py
   Cover the already-initialized skip path.

